Running `polyglot  --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot [-hqv] [--version] [COMMAND]
Polyglot - Multi-language interface generator.
See documentation for more information.
  -h, --help      display usage and exit
  -q              be quiet
  -v              verbose output
      --version   display version and exit
Commands:
  validator  Validate a json proxy
  ada2proxy  Create a proxy for an Ada project. If no unit is explicitly given,
               process all of them.
  proxy2cpp  Create the C++ interface of a proxy representation
  setup      Setup the Polyglot runtime


Running `polyglot setup --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot setup [-hqv] [--check-only] --prefix=<prefixPath>
Setup the Polyglot runtime
      --check-only   do not copy the runtime. Instead, emitt warnings if the
                       runtime was modified.
  -h, --help         display sub-command usage and exit
      --prefix=<prefixPath>
                     installation path
  -q                 be quiet
  -v                 verbose output


Running `polyglot validator --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot validator [-hqv] json_proxy
Validate a json proxy
      json_proxy   json file of the proxy
  -h, --help       display sub-command usage and exit
  -q               be quiet
  -v               verbose output


Running `polyglot ada2proxy --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot ada2proxy [OPTIONS]
Create a proxy for an Ada project. If no unit is explicitly given, process all
of them.
  -P=project_file           input GPR project file
  -o, --output=<outputPath> output path for the proxy project
      --units=<units>       filenames of the units of the input project to bind
  -X=<scenarioVariables>    Scenario variables to pass to the project file
      --RTS=<rts>           Name of the runtime (RTS) to use when loading the
                              project
      --target=<target>     Specify a target for cross platforms
      --with-runtime=<withRuntime>
                            location of the polyglot runtime to use. Defaults
                              to <outputPath>/runtimes.
  -h, --help                display sub-command usage and exit
  -q                        be quiet
  -v                        verbose output


Running `polyglot proxy2cpp --help`
================================================================================

Usage: polyglot proxy2cpp [-hqv] -o=<outputPath> proxy_file
Create the C++ interface of a proxy representation
      proxy_file   input proxy json file
  -h, --help       display sub-command usage and exit
  -o, --output=<outputPath>
                   path to the directory in which the C++ interface should be
                     generated. Directories along the path are created if they
                     do not exist yet.
  -q               be quiet
  -v               verbose output


